{
  "info": {
    "name": "Event Ledger API",
    "_postman_id": "7a8b9c0d-1e2f-3a4b-5c6d-7e8f9a0b1c2d",
    "description": "Full test collection for the Event Ledger system.\n\nEach request is labelled with the step from which it becomes functional.\nRun the [Steps 1-3] folder first to confirm both services are up before anything else.\n\nCollection variables (edit in the Variables tab):\n  gateway_url          — Event Gateway base URL (default: http://localhost:8080)\n  account_service_url  — Account Service base URL (default: http://localhost:8081)\n  test_account_id      — Shared account used across scenarios (default: acct-123)\n\nOut-of-order demonstration:\n  The three CREDIT/DEBIT events in 'POST /events' use timestamps that are NOT\n  in submission order. After submitting all three, GET /events?account= must\n  return them sorted by eventTimestamp (earliest first), not by arrival order.\n    evt-003 → 2026-05-10 (submitted 3rd, earliest timestamp)\n    evt-001 → 2026-05-15 (submitted 1st)\n    evt-002 → 2026-05-16 (submitted 2nd)\n  Expected listing order: evt-003, evt-001, evt-002\n  Expected balance: CREDIT 150 + CREDIT 200 - DEBIT 50 = 300.00",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "gateway_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "description": "Event Gateway base URL"
    },
    {
      "key": "account_service_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8081",
      "description": "Account Service base URL"
    },
    {
      "key": "test_account_id",
      "value": "acct-123",
      "description": "Account ID used across all test scenarios"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "[Steps 1-3] Startup Verification",
      "description": "These two requests work immediately after Steps 1-3.\nBoth services have no custom endpoints yet, so any request returns 404.\nA 404 response from Spring Boot's default error handler confirms the service is running.\nThe test scripts pass as long as the service responds at all.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Gateway — Confirm Running",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gateway_url}}/",
              "host": ["{{gateway_url}}"],
              "path": [""]
            },
            "description": "Available: Steps 1-3 onwards.\n\nSends a GET to the root path. Spring Boot's default error handler returns a 404 JSON response, confirming the service is listening on port 8080.\n\nExpected response (Spring Boot default error):\n{\n  \"timestamp\": \"...\",\n  \"status\": 404,\n  \"error\": \"Not Found\",\n  \"path\": \"/\"\n}"
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Gateway is responding', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 404]);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response is JSON', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('application/json');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Account Service — Confirm Running",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{account_service_url}}/",
              "host": ["{{account_service_url}}"],
              "path": [""]
            },
            "description": "Available: Steps 1-3 onwards.\n\nSends a GET to the root path. A 404 JSON response confirms the Account Service is listening on port 8081.\n\nExpected response (Spring Boot default error):\n{\n  \"timestamp\": \"...\",\n  \"status\": 404,\n  \"error\": \"Not Found\",\n  \"path\": \"/\"\n}"
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Account Service is responding', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 404]);",
                  "});",
                  "",
